WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.835
KL divergence can

00:00:01.647 --> 00:00:02.779
never be negative

00:00:02.918 --> 00:00:04.333
Except in PyTorch

00:00:04.854 --> 00:00:06.127
Many machine-learning

00:00:05.939 --> 00:00:07.412
applications compare

00:00:07.224 --> 00:00:08.639
nearby distributions

00:00:08.793 --> 00:00:09.854
where conventional

00:00:09.665 --> 00:00:11.233
KL formulas lose

00:00:11.045 --> 00:00:11.905
accuracy

00:00:12.430 --> 00:00:14.210
Across 8.5 million

00:00:14.022 --> 00:00:14.717
inputs

00:00:14.789 --> 00:00:16.404
over 85 percent of

00:00:16.298 --> 00:00:18.019
FP32 values had

00:00:17.831 --> 00:00:19.010
at least 1 percent

00:00:18.822 --> 00:00:19.941
relative error near

00:00:19.753 --> 00:00:21.003
tiny divergences

00:00:21.121 --> 00:00:22.665
and about 30 percent

00:00:22.477 --> 00:00:23.585
came out negative

00:00:24.110 --> 00:00:25.265
More precision is

00:00:25.077 --> 00:00:26.020
not the cure

00:00:26.079 --> 00:00:27.211
but strict repairs

00:00:27.035 --> 00:00:28.461
eliminate the significant

00:00:28.296 --> 00:00:30.076
errors on 7.2

00:00:29.888 --> 00:00:31.409
million scored samples

00:00:31.492 --> 00:00:32.742
and correctly round

00:00:32.577 --> 00:00:34.935
all 567 million

00:00:34.747 --> 00:00:35.985
scored components

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:37.524
Full story on

00:00:37.335 --> 00:00:38.231
the dashboard
